From 24aee9e73918e995886bb6e158dbd0cecee6237c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:59:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix(tools): a refused tool names itself and the rule it
 breaks

The project loader refused a tool with unusable numbers as "tool
parameters are not usable: ToolDto { ... }", a debug dump that named
neither the tool nor the field. AddTool, ChangeTool, the library import
and the library reader printed the same dump or a generic line.

New Tool::why_not_sane() (tools::tool_sanity) returns the first rule
broken, in plain words, for example "turning surface speed 0 m/min is
outside 0..2000 m/min (it must be over 0)". Tool::is_sane and
TurningData::is_sane are now why_not_sane().is_none(), so the words and
the verdict cannot drift apart. All four refusals now read
"tool '<name>': <rule>".

The old is_sane bodies are kept verbatim in the tests as an oracle and
swept against the new law: every catalog tool as each kind, 13 fields x
13 edge values, flutes, orientation and turning data. The verdict is
unchanged everywhere.

Fixes #1186

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
